{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "bm00000000000001",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n# Brownian motion\n\nStart with the definition, then distinguish laws and rescaling, drifted models, path roughness, and crossing questions. Each compact node links to its complete explanation.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n布朗运动：从定义出发，依次区分分布与尺度、带漂移模型、路径粗糙性和越界问题。紧凑节点链接到完整讲解。",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -420,
      "width": 4060,
      "height": 260
    },
    {
      "id": "bm00000000000002",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[标准布朗运动|Standard Brownian motion]]\n\nA real process starts at $W_0=0$ a.s.; disjoint-interval increments are mutually independent, and $W_{t+h}-W_t\\sim N(0,h)$ for $t\\ge0,h>0$. Its entire path is continuous on one probability-one event.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n实值过程从零出发，不交区间的零均值 Gaussian 增量相互独立，方差等于时长；同一个概率一事件上整条路径连续。增量平稳，水平分布不平稳。",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 4060,
      "height": 230,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm00000000000003",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[布朗有限维分布|Brownian finite-dimensional laws]]\n\nEvery finite observation vector is jointly Gaussian with mean zero and covariance $\\Sigma_{ij}=\\min(t_i,t_j)$. Repeated times or time zero can make $\\Sigma$ singular; a full-dimensional density then does not apply.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n任意有限时刻向量联合 Gaussian，均值零、协方差为两时刻的较小者。零时刻或重复时刻可导致退化，不能套非退化密度。",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 290,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm00000000000004",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[布朗尺度变换|Brownian scaling]]\n\nFor a fixed finite $c>0$, $Y_t=W_{ct}/\\sqrt c$ is standard Brownian motion. This preserves the law of continuous paths; it does not identify the original and rescaled curves.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n预先固定有限 $c>0$，时间加快 $c$ 倍、空间除以 $\\sqrt c$ 后仍为标准布朗运动。这是连续路径的律相同，不是同一路径上的相等。",
      "x": 700,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm00000000000005",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[带漂移布朗运动|Brownian motion with drift]]\n\n$X_t=x+\\mu t+\\sigma W_t$, with fixed real $x,\\mu$ and $\\sigma>0$. The mean is $x+\\mu t$ and variance is $\\sigma^2t$. Setting $\\sigma=0$ is a separate deterministic extension.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n$x,\\mu$ 为固定实数，$\\sigma>0$。起点、平均漂移与随机尺度分开；方差为 $\\sigma^2t$，$\\sigma=0$ 时另退化为确定直线。",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm00000000000006",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[布朗路径处处不可导|Nowhere differentiable paths]]\n\nOn one probability-one event, no time has a finite derivative. At zero use the right-hand limit. A fixed-time statement alone does not establish this simultaneous claim.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n同一个概率一事件上，每个时刻都没有有限导数；零时刻采用右侧极限。逐个固定时刻的概率一陈述不能直接替代此同时结论。",
      "x": 2100,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm00000000000007",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[布朗反射原理|Reflection principle]]\n\nFor standard Brownian motion, fixed $t>0,a>0$ and $M_t=\\sup_{0\\le s\\le t}W_s$,\n$$P(M_t\\ge a)=2P(W_t\\ge a).$$\nReflect after the first hit; crossing before $t$ is different from ending above $a$. The formula does not generally apply with drift.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n对标准布朗运动、固定 $t>0,a>0$，途中越过 $a$ 的概率是终点超过它的两倍。首次触及时反射余下路径；有漂移时不能直接照用此式。",
      "x": 3500,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm00000000000008",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[协方差核刻画布朗运动|Gaussian characterization]]\n\nA centered real Gaussian process on $t\\ge0$ with covariance $\\min(s,t)$ has Brownian finite-dimensional laws and a continuous modification. The current version is Brownian only when its own paths are a.s. continuous.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n中心实 Gaussian 过程的该核给出布朗有限维律，且存在连续修正版本；当前版本仍须自身路径几乎必然连续。只给均值与核不能替代 Gaussian 假设。",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 700,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm00000000000009",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[带漂移布朗增量|Drifted increment law]]\n\nFor fixed $s\\ge0,h>0$, $X_{s+h}-X_s\\sim N(\\mu h,\\sigma^2h)$. Fixed disjoint intervals give mutually independent increments; overlapping windows need not. The standard deviation is $\\sigma\\sqrt h$.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n固定起点与长度的增量均值为 $\\mu h$、方差为 $\\sigma^2h$；标准差为 $\\sigma\\sqrt h$。预先固定的不交区间增量相互独立，重叠窗口未必独立。",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": 700,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm0000000000000a",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[布朗路径无限总变差|Infinite total variation]]\n\nOn one probability-one event, every interval $0\\le a<b<\\infty$ has infinite total variation. This concerns absolute changes over all finite partitions, not a quadratic-variation limit.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n同一个概率一事件覆盖全部 $0\\le a<b<\\infty$ 区间。这里对所有有限分割的绝对增量和取上确界，与二次变差的分割极限不同。",
      "x": 2100,
      "y": 700,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm0000000000000b",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[鞅与停时.canvas|Information and stopping times]]\n\nCap the first hit at a fixed deadline to get a bounded stopping time. The [[布朗强Markov性|Brownian strong Markov theorem]] supplies independent restarted motion; deterministic-time independence alone does not.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n把首次触及时刻截断在固定期限，得到布朗自然信息下的有界停时。[[布朗强Markov性]]提供独立重启依据，不能只引用固定时刻的独立增量。",
      "x": 3500,
      "y": 700,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300
    },
    {
      "id": "bm0000000000000c",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[布朗运动不平稳|Levels versus increments]]\n\n$\\operatorname{Var}(W_t)=t$ rules out strict and weak stationarity of the levels. Fixed-length increments have shift-invariant joint laws; overlapping increments can still be dependent.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n水平方差随时间增长，既不严平稳也不宽平稳。固定长度增量的联合律可随起点平移保持不变，但重叠增量仍可能依赖。",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1060,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm0000000000000d",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[布朗二次变差|Quadratic variation]]\n\nFor fixed $T>0$ and deterministic partitions of $[0,T]$ with vanishing mesh, the squared-increment sum tends to $T$ in $L^2$. Almost-sure convergence holds for dyadic refinements, and more generally nested such partitions. Arbitrary path-chosen grids are not included.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n固定区间上，确定性分割网格趋零时，增量平方和均方趋于 $T$。二进细分及更一般的嵌套分割给出几乎必然收敛；不声称所有看过路径再选的网格都适用。",
      "x": 2100,
      "y": 1060,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 330,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "bm0000000000000e",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## Next: stochastic integration\n\nThe nonzero Brownian quadratic-variation limit motivates a second-order term in stochastic change-of-variable formulas. The precise Itô integral and formula belong to the next topic.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n布朗二次变差的非零极限说明随机换元公式为何会出现二阶项；Itô 积分与公式的准确条件属于后续主题。",
      "x": 2800,
      "y": 1060,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 240,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0067-total-variation",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2800,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[函数总变差|Total variation of a function]]\n\nFor a real function on a finite interval $[a,b]$, $a<b$, add absolute increments on a finite partition, then take the supremum over all such partitions. BV means this supremum is finite. A rise from 0 to 1 and back has net change 0 but variation 2.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n有限区间上实值函数的有限分割，先累加绝对增量，再对全部分割取上确界。上确界有限才是有界变差；上升一单位再下降一单位，净变化零、变差为二。"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0067-bv-derivative",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2800,
      "y": 700,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[有界变差函数几乎处处可导|BV and almost-everywhere derivatives]]\n\nA real BV function on $[a,b]$, $a<b$, has a finite derivative at Lebesgue-almost every interior time. Nowhere differentiability therefore rules out BV. Infinite variation does not give the converse.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n实值有界变差函数在区间内部几乎处处有有限导数；这里是时间的勒贝格零测集。因此处处不可导排除有界变差，反向推断不成立。"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0067-brownian-strong-markov",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3500,
      "y": 1060,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 350,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[布朗强Markov性|Brownian strong Markov property]]\n\nFor standard Brownian motion and an a.s.-finite stopping time $\\tau$ for its natural filtration, $(W_{\\tau+s}-W_\\tau)_{s\\ge0}$ is standard Brownian motion independent of the information available at $\\tau$. For reflection, cap the first-hit time at the fixed deadline.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n标准布朗运动在自然滤过的几乎必然有限停时后，减去当前位置得到新的标准布朗运动，且独立于停时已知信息。反射证明可用有界停时 $\\tau_a\\wedge t$。"
    }
  ],
